{"title":"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(overkill)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (overkill)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Stars_and_Bars)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Stars and Bars)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Similar_to_above,_using_number_separation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Similar to above, using number separation)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Sohil_Rathi\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Sohil Rathi</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fair standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided dice are thrown, the probability that the sum of the numbers on the top faces is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac603cdac4dfed9654cab1540ba3f1927ef6202.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n}{6^{7}},\\]\" width=\"22\" height=\"32\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663fec0d21906a8e88f8ade54cbda0edc918880d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }42\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }49\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }56\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }63\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }84\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Add possibilities. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, listed below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cefc61e6c6c3c579f41fa9439d609bc37378316a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4,1,1,1,1,1,1: \\dbinom{7}{6} = 7\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/9857a5f11a0c04b33b0aebaf4b6a7d088214feb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3,2,1,1,1,1,1: \\dbinom{7}{5}\\dbinom{2}{1} = 42\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb2c3abd05eac4a275b16190916b3affa5373f36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2,2,2,1,1,1,1: \\dbinom{7}{4} = 35.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Add up the possibilities: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b11044edcc86997740ffb921e47529b9db9209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35+42+7=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }  84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"177\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Rolling a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> with 7 dice can be represented with stars and bars, with 10 stars and 6 bars. Each star represents one of the dots on the dices' faces and the bars represent separation between different dice. However, we must note that each die must have at least one dot on a face, so there must already be 7 stars predetermined. We are left with 3 stars and 6 bars, which we can rearrange in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/6/d56e7856f4cac7dac3d37c356eadb2022901e8dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{9}{3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28overkill.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(overkill)\">Solution 3 (overkill)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (overkill)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can use generating functions, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275c784b05073d53da74fa56c1ca7681f83834e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+x^2+...+x^6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" /> is the function for each die. We want to find the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb2b080e28bf22191584d4b8d20a6187c8f3192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{10}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e805af9ddbeff588bb7e514772f55f8a56ba9db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+x^2+...+x^6)^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"19\" />, which is the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974630844d19daf1576d7a8bd081ccc4feef8d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1-x^7}{1-x}\\right)^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"86\" height=\"47\" />. This evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c34f4ed88091e20792bea226bce05f758eb7c446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{-7}{3} \\cdot (-1)^3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"199\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Stars_and_Bars.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Stars_and_Bars)\">Solution 4 (Stars and Bars)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Stars and Bars)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If we let each number take its minimum value of 1, we will get 7 as the minimum sum. So we can do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to find the number of balls we need to distribute to get three more added to the minimum to get 10, so the problem is asking how many ways can you put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes. From there we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/122900be539152782e1ee85292f85b58b0ed8517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{7+3-1}{7-1}=\\binom{9}{6}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"251\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Similar_to_above.2C_using_number_separation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Similar_to_above,_using_number_separation)\">Solution 5 (Similar to above, using number separation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Similar to above, using number separation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can use number separation for this problem. If we set each of the dice value to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015c8090f36c8dd971a8acf302e9b7a03546ece2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D\\{a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />, we can say \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fa8d89fc5f1ea2ae81c6eff11563abe00d1988.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />'s elements are larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using the positive number separation formula, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/f/f1f7299be5e74367e76d23d995d5c12efadec438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n-1}{r-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"66\" height=\"53\" />, we can make the following equations. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a2d989d668f6fde0051a947d9145892516552.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} D &amp;= 10 \\\\ a+b+c+d+e+f+g &amp;= 10 \\\\ \\dbinom{10-1}{7-1} &amp;= \\\\ \\dbinom{9}{6} &amp;= \\\\ \\dbinom{9}{3} &amp;= \\\\ \\dfrac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7}{3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1} &amp;= \\\\ 12 \\cdot 7 &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }84} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"284\" height=\"301\" />\n</p><p>Note: We are unable to use non-negative number separations due to the fact that the dice *must* be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or positive.\n</p><p>~ Wiselion =)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gTpg8yInCCY\">https://youtu.be/gTpg8yInCCY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HVn1WV80ZIU\">https://youtu.be/HVn1WV80ZIU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Sohil_Rathi\">Video Solution by Sohil Rathi</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Sohil Rathi\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This video by Sohil Rathi explains the solution using two methods: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">Casework</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ball-and-urn\" title=\"Ball-and-urn\">Stars &amp; Bars</a>.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5UojVH4Cqqs&amp;t=5381s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5UojVH4Cqqs&amp;t=5381s</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14 is Sohil Rathi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-br